35,2,1,talk,Mio,,"It looks like we have plenty of software expertise on the board, but finding field crews is a nightmare.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,George,,"Interestingly, our best exits were quiet back-office tools. The ones with physical premises were the ones we lost.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"We're spending follow-on money way too fast, and our credit line is useless for subscription-based security.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Hardware and depots are killing our audit timeline. Software is much easier to report, though less verifiable.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,Security reviews for medical or financial data are taking forever. Hardware delivery is also a huge gamble.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@May, if the credit line doesn't like subscriptions, does that mean we should avoid SaaS?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,George,,"@Mio, the data shows SaaS retention is actually lower for some, but the exits are cleaner.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,It means we need to be careful about how we fund the growth phase.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Mizuki, does the security review time apply to the medical candidates?","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"Yes, it's a significant bottleneck for anything handling medical records.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@George, which candidates have the best retention based on what you saw?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,George,,The ones with field instruments and independent practices are holding strong.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,We need something that doesn't drain our reserves instantly.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,And something that doesn't make the quarter-end audit a nightmare.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,So we want to avoid long security reviews and hardware shortages.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
